      "comment": "DIAMONDINTHEROUGH (2) produced an encouraging effort when he came from this barrier and finished less than 5 metres away in third at Newcastle at his first run back from a 10-month spell. Fitter for that and is likely to get all the favours so has winning claims. TIGER TIGER (1) has been competitive of late and kept the ball rolling last time when 4 metres from the winner in second at Bathurst. No excuses from this advantageous draw. Big chance. ROCK WHAT YOU ARE (5) broke through at Young last time. Draws a couple of spots wider but could go on with it. WORTH EVERY CENT (4) broke when resuming but will be fitter and is better placed coming back to a maiden. REVERSE SWING (3) draws much better than he did on debut so looks a likely improver. ",
